<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wampanoag Tribe of Gay Head (Aquinnah)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aquinnah Wampanoag</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wampanoag Tribe of Gay Head (Aquinnah) is a Native American tribe based at Aquinnah, formerly Gay Head, at the western end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marthas-vineyard">Martha's Vineyard</a> in Massachusetts. Its members descend from the Wampanoag communities of the island, who kept part of their land through the colonial period. The tribe received federal recognition from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1987.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wampanoag-tribe-of-gay-head-aquinnah.jpg" alt="Wampanoag Tribe of Gay Head (Aquinnah)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alberto Fernandez Fernandez · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gay_Head_Cliffs_-_Aquinnah_-_Martha%27s_Vineyard_-_MA_-_USA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
